      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it feels like a bit of an unfair characterization to call it a \"serious internal challenge\" if the theory is actually used by experts to find objective answers. if a judge is actually following the text and the history, isn't it still a legitimate legal method even if people don't like the outcome? it feels like some people just want to ignore the Constitution whenever it doesn't align with modern views.",
